{% extends "layouts/base.html.twig" %}

{% block title %}Privacy Policy - {{ app_name }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow px-6 py-8 sm:px-10">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">Last updated: {{ last_updated }}</p>

        <div class="prose prose-blue max-w-none">
            <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
            <p>
                {{ app_name }} is a financial management service for UK charities, operated by 
                <strong>Portobello Community Media SCIO</strong> (Scottish Charity Number SC053184).
            </p>
            <p>
                This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect personal data when you use our service.
                We are committed to protecting your privacy and complying with the UK General Data Protection Regulation 
                (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018.
            </p>

            <h2>2. Our Role</h2>
            <p>
                When charities use {{ app_name }} to manage their financial records:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>The charity</strong> is the <em>Data Controller</em> – they decide what data to collect about their donors, members, and transactions</li>
                <li><strong>Portobello Community Media SCIO</strong> is the <em>Data Processor</em> – we process data on behalf of the charity according to their instructions</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                For data about users who log into {{ app_name }} (charity staff/volunteers), we act as a Data Controller.
            </p>

            <h2>3. What Data We Collect</h2>
            
            <h3>3.1 User Account Data (we are Controller)</h3>
            <p>When you create an account or log in, we collect:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Name and email address (from your OAuth provider (for example Google or Microsoft))</li>
                <li>Login history and session information</li>
                <li>Actions you perform within the system (audit logs)</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>3.2 Charity Data (charity is Controller, we are Processor)</h3>
            <p>Charities may store the following in {{ app_name }}:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Donor information:</strong> Names, addresses, contact details, Gift Aid declarations</li>
                <li><strong>Member information:</strong> Names, contact details, membership status, trustee roles</li>
                <li><strong>Financial transactions:</strong> Amounts, dates, categories, descriptions</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="min-w-full">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th class="text-left">Data Type</th>
                        <th class="text-left">Legal Basis</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>User account data</td>
                        <td>Legitimate interests (providing the service you requested)</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Login/security logs</td>
                        <td>Legitimate interests (security and fraud prevention)</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Charity financial data</td>
                        <td>Contract (processing agreement with the charity)</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Donor/member data</td>
                        <td>Contract (processing on charity's instructions)</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            </div>

            <h2>5. How We Use Your Data</h2>
            <p>We use personal data to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Provide and maintain the {{ app_name }} service</li>
                <li>Authenticate users and manage access permissions</li>
                <li>Generate financial reports for charities</li>
                <li>Process Gift Aid claims on behalf of charities</li>
                <li>Maintain security and prevent unauthorised access</li>
                <li>Comply with legal obligations (e.g., HMRC record-keeping requirements)</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We do <strong>not</strong>:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Sell personal data to third parties</li>
                <li>Use personal data for marketing purposes</li>
                <li>Make automated decisions that significantly affect individuals</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
            <p>We retain data for the following periods:</p>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="min-w-full">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th class="text-left">Data Type</th>
                        <th class="text-left">Retention Period</th>
                        <th class="text-left">Reason</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Financial records</td>
                        <td>7 years</td>
                        <td>HMRC requirements for Gift Aid</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Gift Aid declarations</td>
                        <td>7 years after last donation</td>
                        <td>HMRC requirements</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Audit logs</td>
                        <td>7 years</td>
                        <td>Financial accountability</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>User account data</td>
                        <td>7 years after account closure</td>
                        <td>Legal and audit requirements</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Session/login data</td>
                        <td>90 days</td>
                        <td>Security monitoring</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            </div>

            <h2>7. Data Sharing and International Transfers</h2>
            <p>We may share data with:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>OAuth providers</strong> (for example Google, Microsoft) – for authentication only</li>
                <li><strong>Hosting provider</strong> – our servers are currently hosted in the United States</li>
                <li><strong>Law enforcement</strong> – if required by law or court order</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>International Data Transfers</h3>
            <p>
                Our hosting infrastructure is located in the United States. The US does not have an adequacy 
                decision from the UK, so we rely on Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) and our hosting 
                provider's Data Processing Agreement to ensure appropriate safeguards for your data.
            </p>
            <p>
                We are evaluating UK/EEA-based hosting options and may migrate in the future to keep data 
                within jurisdictions with adequate data protection standards.
            </p>

            <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
            <p>Under UK GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Access</strong> – Request a copy of your personal data</li>
                <li><strong>Rectification</strong> – Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
                <li><strong>Erasure</strong> – Request deletion of your data (subject to retention requirements)</li>
                <li><strong>Restriction</strong> – Request limitation of processing</li>
                <li><strong>Portability</strong> – Receive your data in a portable format</li>
                <li><strong>Object</strong> – Object to processing based on legitimate interests</li>
            </ul>
            
            <h3>For Charity Users</h3>
            <p>
                If you are a user of {{ app_name }} (charity staff/volunteer), contact us directly to exercise your rights.
            </p>
            
            <h3>For Donors/Members</h3>
            <p>
                If you are a donor or member of a charity using {{ app_name }}, please contact that charity directly. 
                They are the Data Controller for your information. The charity can use our built-in tools to:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Export all data held about you (Subject Access Request)</li>
                <li>Delete or anonymise your data (Right to Erasure)</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>9. Security</h2>
            <p>We protect your data through:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Encryption in transit (HTTPS/TLS)</li>
                <li>Secure authentication via OAuth 2.0</li>
                <li>Role-based access controls within each charity</li>
                <li>Audit logging of all data access and changes</li>
                <li>Regular security reviews</li>
                <li>Re-authentication required for sensitive actions</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>10. Cookies</h2>
            <p>
                {{ app_name }} uses only essential cookies required for the service to function:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Session cookie</strong> – Maintains your login session</li>
                <li><strong>CSRF token</strong> – Prevents cross-site request forgery attacks</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                We do not use tracking cookies, analytics cookies, or advertising cookies.
            </p>

            <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p>
                We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify users of significant changes 
                by displaying a notice within the application.
            </p>

            <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
            <p>For privacy enquiries or to exercise your rights, contact:</p>
            <address class="not-italic">
                <strong>Portobello Community Media SCIO</strong><br>
                Scottish Charity Number: SC053184<br>
                Email: &#99;&#111;&#110;&#116;&#97;&#99;&#116;&#64;&#112;&#111;&#114;&#116;&#111;&#98;&#101;&#108;&#108;&#111;&#99;&#111;&#109;&#109;&#117;&#110;&#105;&#116;&#121;&#109;&#101;&#100;&#105;&#97;&#46;&#111;&#114;&#103;<br>
            </address>

            <h2>13. Complaints</h2>
            <p>
                If you are not satisfied with our response to a privacy concern, you have the right to lodge a 
                complaint with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO):
            </p>
            <address class="not-italic">
                Information Commissioner's Office<br>
                Wycliffe House, Water Lane<br>
                Wilmslow, Cheshire SK9 5AF<br>
                Website: <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a><br>
                Helpline: 0303 123 1113
            </address>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200">
            <a href="/login" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">&larr; Back to login</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
